---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Salary to hourly calculator: what a yearly salary pays per hour"
  description="Turn a yearly salary into an hourly, weekly and monthly rate, or turn an hourly wage back into a yearly salary. Based on the hours you actually work."
>
  <h1>Salary to hourly calculator</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A salary of 60,000 a year sounds precise until someone asks what it pays an hour. This
    page does that division honestly: by the hours you actually work, not by a made up round
    number.
  </p>
    <figure class="fig fig--money"><img src="/img/salary.webp" alt="United States dollar bills spread out" width="1200" height="514" decoding="async"></figure>
    <nav class="onpage" aria-label="On this page"><p class="onpage-title">On this page</p><ul><li><a href="#the-working">The working</a></li><li><a href="#common-salaries-converted">Common salaries, converted</a></li><li><a href="#questions-people-ask">Questions people ask</a></li></ul></nav>

  <div class="sheet">
    <div class="field-grid">
      <div>
        <label for="mode">I know my</label>
        <select id="mode">
          <option value="salary">Yearly salary</option>
          <option value="hourly">Hourly wage</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="amount" id="amount-label">Yearly salary</label>
        <input type="number" id="amount" inputmode="decimal" min="0" step="any" value="60000" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="hours">Hours worked per week</label>
        <input type="number" id="hours" inputmode="decimal" min="1" max="112" step="any" value="40" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="weeks">Weeks worked per year</label>
        <input type="number" id="weeks" inputmode="decimal" min="1" max="52" step="any" value="52" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <button class="btn btn--primary" id="calc" type="button">Convert it</button>
    <div id="out" aria-live="polite" style="margin-top:1.5rem;"></div>
    <p class="result-note">
      All figures are before tax. Weeks worked per year is 52 if you are paid through your
      holidays, which most salaried staff are. If you are unpaid for time off, put the weeks
      you actually work, often 48 or 49, and the hourly figure will come out higher, because
      it is the honest one.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="the-working">The working</h2>
  <p>
    Hourly pay = yearly salary ÷ (hours per week × weeks per year). The standard full time
    assumption, 40 hours for 52 weeks, is 2,080 hours, and most quoted conversions use it.
    US federal staff use 2,087 hours, the average accounting for leap years, which is why
    government tables differ by a few cents. This page uses your numbers, so part time and
    term time work come out right too.
  </p>

  <h2 id="common-salaries-converted">Common salaries, converted</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Yearly salary</th><th scope="col" class="num">Per hour</th><th scope="col" class="num">Per week</th><th scope="col" class="num">Per month</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>30,000</td><td class="num">14.42</td><td class="num">576.92</td><td class="num">2,500.00</td></tr>
      <tr><td>45,000</td><td class="num">21.63</td><td class="num">865.38</td><td class="num">3,750.00</td></tr>
      <tr class="point"><td>60,000</td><td class="num">28.85</td><td class="num">1,153.85</td><td class="num">5,000.00</td></tr>
      <tr><td>75,000</td><td class="num">36.06</td><td class="num">1,442.31</td><td class="num">6,250.00</td></tr>
      <tr><td>100,000</td><td class="num">48.08</td><td class="num">1,923.08</td><td class="num">8,333.33</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>At 40 hours a week, 52 weeks a year, before tax. Monthly is the salary divided by 12.</p>

  <h2 id="questions-people-ask">Questions people ask</h2>
  <dl class="faq">
    <dt>Why does my payslip show a different hourly rate?</dt>
    <dd>
      Employers often divide by contracted hours only, or by 52.14 weeks, or they build
      overtime and allowances into the rate. If your contract states an hourly rate, that one
      governs. This page is for comparing offers and checking your own arithmetic.
    </dd>
    <dt>How do I compare a salary with a freelance day rate?</dt>
    <dd>
      Convert the salary to a day rate first (weekly ÷ days worked per week), then remember
      the freelancer gets no paid holiday, pension contribution, sick pay or employer tax
      paid for them. A common rule of thumb is that a day rate needs to be roughly double
      the salaried day rate to come out even.
    </dd>
    <dt>What about overtime at time and a half?</dt>
    <dd>
      Multiply your hourly figure by 1.5 for those hours. Ten extra hours a week at 28.85 is
      432.75 before tax. Check your contract, though: many salaried contracts pay no overtime
      at all, which quietly lowers the real hourly rate, and this calculator will show it if
      you put the true hours in.
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <p class="meta">Method: salary divided by hours per week times weeks per year; 2,080 hours is the standard full time year. Page last checked 13 November 2026.</p>

  <script>
    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
    const out = $('out');
    const money = (n) => n.toLocaleString('en-GB', { minimumFractionDigits: 2, maximumFractionDigits: 2 });

    $('mode').addEventListener('change', () => {
      $('amount-label').textContent = $('mode').value === 'salary' ? 'Yearly salary' : 'Hourly wage';
      compute();
    });

    function compute() {
      const amount = parseFloat($('amount').value) || 0;
      const hours = parseFloat($('hours').value) || 40;
      const weeks = parseFloat($('weeks').value) || 52;
      const yearHours = hours * weeks;
      const yearly = $('mode').value === 'salary' ? amount : amount * yearHours;
      const hourly = yearHours ? yearly / yearHours : 0;
      out.innerHTML =
        '<p class="result-figure">' + money(hourly) + ' an hour</p>' +
        '<table><tbody>' +
        '<tr><td>Per hour</td><td class="num">' + money(hourly) + '</td></tr>' +
        '<tr><td>Per day (' + hours / 5 + ' hours)</td><td class="num">' + money(hourly * hours / 5) + '</td></tr>' +
        '<tr><td>Per week</td><td class="num">' + money(hourly * hours) + '</td></tr>' +
        '<tr><td>Per month</td><td class="num">' + money(yearly / 12) + '</td></tr>' +
        '<tr><td>Per year</td><td class="num">' + money(yearly) + '</td></tr>' +
        '</tbody></table>' +
        '<p class="result-note">Based on ' + hours + ' hours a week for ' + weeks + ' weeks, ' + yearHours.toLocaleString('en-GB') + ' hours a year, before tax.</p>';
    }

    $('calc').addEventListener('click', compute);
    compute();
  </script>
</Base>
